{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 24,
      "name": "Collapsing Bridge",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "The whole idea is one number (how fast the collapse chases you) set against the bridge's shape, and every layout has to be checked so a normal runner who jumps every gap still stays ahead. That check is easy by hand per layout, and 18 shapes cover the idea. Climbing chases were left to Rising Goo (idea 12), so this bridge stays mostly level: the chase comes from behind, not from below.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "motion kind 'melt': a part fades and drops away, then comes back after 'away' seconds",
          "'step' parts in walking order, with tests for gap (at most 6) and rise (at most 3.5) at rest",
          "fall or hazard touch sends you back to the start pad; course built per client, so each runner sees their own collapse",
          "red see-through hazard parts, jelly connectors at both ends"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "Motion kind 'collapse': each piece cracks, then drops at headStart + (its distance along the path) / speed, counted from the 'section entry clock' (idea 11; the same per-player step trigger as ideas 3, 10, 12 and 25, built once). Speed can be a curve (start speed, end speed), the same curve format as Rising Goo's flood (idea 12). Not the same as 'melt': pieces fall on a wave behind you, not when you touch them",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "Crack look: reuse Melting Floor's shared crack / melt warning look (idea 2, ObbyFx), shown on the piece about 0.8 s before it drops. New here only: a low rumble that gets louder as the wave front nears you, and a crunch plus dust puff when a piece falls",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Rest island: a grey stone pad with a glowing ring (same look as Rising Goo's rest ledges, idea 12) that pauses the wave while you stand on it, for at most N seconds as the ring drains; the wave goes on when you step off or the ring runs out",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Bridge resets for you when you go back to the start pad (all pieces back, clock cleared); the same reset Melting Floor's 'gone until start pad' tiles use (idea 2)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Path distance for bends and forks: the wave follows the walking path (sum of step distances), per branch on a fork, so turns, S-bends and split bridges fall in the right order. Optional side offset so one half of a wide bridge can fall a little earlier (Two Halves)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Boost planks (Boost Plank, Boost or Bust): reuse Speed Strip's client boost controller, chevron look and boost test rule (idea 16); nothing new",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Hazard puddles (Goo Spots): the shared 'hazard touch = back to the start pad' from Crusher Alley (idea 1)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Runner test: for every layout, a runner at 16 studs/s (or the boost speed on boost planks) who loses 0.15 s per jump and 0.3 s per turn must stay at least 1 s ahead of the wave at every piece, on every branch. Crusher Alley (1) and Rising Goo (12) reuse this runner",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "The bridge is plank wood with a big crack line painted on the first plank, and as soon as you step on, you hear a rumble and see pieces behind you darken, crack and drop. Rest islands are grey stone with a green ring, so they read as safe.",
      "generator": null,
